// exp1c_variants_r4.zag -- EXP1c 12 world variants, retune iteration 4
// (frozen 2026-09-27, implemented wave-20260927-1421pdt under PREREG_EXP1c M5).
// Discard reason for iteration 3 (frozen criteria only): C1 FAIL
// (median ward-turtle 649 < 960, VOID) and C3 FAIL (0 of 4 scripted
// strategies >= 720). C2 passed (median Z 45 < 300).
// Diagnosis: iteration 3's stationary single-cell motes fixed P's
// futile-chase (ward-turtle 649, 6 variants at 1200) but broke lamp-farm
// (672, 6 variants died at ticks 51-145 during setup). Root cause: with
// only 2 distinct stationary cells, lamp-farm's setup (which takes a mote
// for the lamp) can find all local motes dormant after opportunistic
// eats, leaving no active mote to take; it then wanders and starves.
// Retune (within the inherited frozen rules): the 4 local motes remain
// single-cell stationary ranges (necessary for C1, as proven in the
// iteration 3 header), but are now placed at 4 DISTINCT cells near home.
// This guarantees an active mote remains available for lamp-farm's
// take-for-lamp setup even after opportunistic eats. The 2 deep motes
// (past the void) retain moving ranges; void/start/home/crystals/storms
// unchanged from iteration 3. All frozen rules re-verified by
// v6_badmot/v6_badworld.
// Reuses VParams/v_apply from variants.zag; physics from world.zag unchanged.

@import("variants.zag")

fn v6_fill(v:i32, p:*VParams)i32 {
